From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Matt Graham <matt.sg@hotmail.com>
Date: Sun, 25 Oct 2026 19:25:15 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 04/12] apu: DSP56300 GP/EP, threaded frames, deeper device
 queue

The real DSP (src/apu/dsp) runs the title's GP and EP programs on their own
thread and replaces the doorbell acknowledgement. The front-end queue lock
is made once per process. Audio output keeps upstream's queue pacing with a
1024 x 8 default, deep enough for whole DSP periods.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
